    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The investment plan presents a genuinely balanced case for JPM. The bull case rests on a confirmed uptrend with aligned moving averages (Price > 10 EMA > 50 SMA > 200 SMA), strong balance sheet fundamentals ($3.875T assets, $327.9B equity), and price holding near 60-day highs. However, the bear case highlights real concerns: MACD histogram contraction of 58%, RSI pulling back from extreme overbought levels, declining relative volume at 0.82, and a materially unfavorable risk/reward at current levels (~2.1% upside to upper Bollinger Band vs ~6.5% downside to 50 SMA). Critically, income statement, news, sentiment, and macro data are all unavailable, creating a material information gap for a bank whose earnings are driven by net interest income, credit conditions, and Fed policy. With neither side having a decisive edge and the stock extended 22% above the 200 SMA, Hold is the honest and appropriate call. No new entries should be initiated at current levels ($178.59); wait for either a pullback to the $167-$170 zone or a confirmed breakout above $182.28 on above-average volume.\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain existing positions; do not add at current levels. If a pullback entry becomes available near $167-$170, size at roughly half of full allocation given the incomplete fundamental picture.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
